5. Scope
5.1 Systems Included in Scope
The redesign shall include:
•	reactor core simulation;
•	reactor state management;
•	annihilation-stage simulation;
•	dark-fusion-stage simulation;
•	containment-field simulation;
•	stabilizer simulation;
•	director-beam alignment;
•	six Dark Fusion Catalyzers;
•	superstructure integrity;
•	thermal and waste-heat simulation;
•	secondary thermal plant logic;
•	fuel-cell handling;
•	matter and antimatter management;
•	fuel enrichment towers;
•	reactor startup and shutdown;
•	automatic and manual operation;
•	failure and disaster handling;
•	DECAOS announcements;
•	DECAOS subtitles;
•	alarms and warning states;
•	dynamic background music;
•	reactive event timelines;
•	map effects and cinematic sequences;
•	control-room displays;
•	power quotas and scoring;
•	ending conditions;
•	save, reset, or round-restart behavior, if required by the final gameplay format.
5.2 Existing Systems to Replace
The following Source I/O systems shall be replaced or substantially controlled by Lua:
•	reactor core simulation;
•	reactor subsystem logic;
•	Dark Fusion Catalyzers;
•	Dark Fusion Fuel Enrichment Towers;
•	prop_coreball control;
•	DECAOS announcement logic;
•	cinematic event sequences;
•	background music control.
5.3 Existing Systems to Retain
The following systems may remain controlled by Source I/O unless later integration becomes necessary:
•	passing trains;
•	small ship sequences;
•	minor environmental scene controllers;
•	secret triggers;
•	unrelated ambient events.
5.4 Scope Boundary
Lua shall be treated as the authoritative source for reactor state.
Map entities may display, animate, emit effects, or receive commands, but shall not independently determine the authoritative reactor state unless explicitly documented as a retained legacy system.
