7. Assumptions and Constraints
7.1 Technical Constraints
The system shall operate within Garry’s Mod and Source Engine limitations.
The implementation shall account for:
•	server and client Lua separation;
•	networked-variable bandwidth;
•	entity limits;
•	map entity naming;
•	Source Engine animation and I/O behavior;
•	multiplayer synchronization;
•	late-joining clients;
•	Lua errors and invalid entity references;
•	variable frame rates and server tick rates;
•	Workshop distribution limitations;
•	compatibility with the compiled map and available VMF entities.
7.2 Design Constraints
The reactor shall remain understandable enough that a player can learn it through displays, feedback, subtitles, experimentation, and documentation.
The reactor shall not rely exclusively on hidden variables.
Important unsafe conditions shall have at least one observable indication before they become irreversible, unless the condition is intentionally designed as a hidden event.
7.3 Fictional-Physics Constraint
The simulation may use fictional physics, but each modeled variable shall have:
•	a defined meaning;
•	a defined unit or normalized range;
•	one or more sources;
•	one or more effects;
•	valid minimum and maximum values;
•	behavior when outside the intended operating range.
