2.	Reactor Core Simulation
3.	Annihilation System
4.	Dark Fusion System
5.	Stabilizer and Containment System
6.	Director Beam System
7.	Catalyzer Controller
8.	Superstructure and Damage System
9.	Thermal Plant System
10.	Fuel and Enrichment System
11.	Power Export and Quota System
12.	DECAOS Controller
13.	Alarm and Notification System
14.	Timeline and Sequence Controller
15.	Music Controller
16.	Map Entity Integration Layer
17.	Instrumentation and 3D2D Display Layer
18.	Scoring and Ending Controller
19.	Debugging and Administration Interface
8.2 Authoritative State
SYS-ARCH-001
The server shall own the authoritative reactor simulation state.
SYS-ARCH-002
Clients shall receive only the reactor data required for displays, effects, sound, and interaction feedback.
SYS-ARCH-003
A client shall not be able to directly assign authoritative reactor values.
SYS-ARCH-004
All control interactions shall be validated by the server before changing reactor state.
SYS-ARCH-005
The system shall provide a defined update interval for simulation calculations.
SYS-ARCH-006
Simulation behavior shall not materially change with graphical frame rate.
8.3 Module Communication
Modules should communicate using documented Luasquare inputs, outputs, events, or shared interfaces.
Direct modification of another module’s internal variables should be avoided unless the variable is explicitly defined as shared state.
Each module shall document:
•	inputs;
•	outputs;
•	internal state;
•	update frequency;
•	generated events;
•	accepted commands;
•	fault states;
•	reset behavior.
