9. Reactor State Model
9.1 Required Top-Level States
The reactor shall support at least the following top-level states:
•	OFFLINE
•	STARTUP_AUTHORIZATION
•	STARTUP_DEPLOYMENT
•	ANNIHILATION_STAGE
•	DARK_FUSION_IGNITION
•	DARK_FUSION_STAGE
•	STALLING
•	NORMAL_SHUTDOWN
•	EMERGENCY_SHUTDOWN
•	MELTDOWN_STAGE_1
•	MELTDOWN_STAGE_2
•	MELTDOWN_STAGE_3
•	PURGE_SEQUENCE
•	SINGULARITY_BREACH
•	ENDING
•	RESETTING
Additional substates may be added where required.
9.2 State Transition Requirements
STATE-001
Every top-level state shall define its valid entry conditions.
STATE-002
Every top-level state shall define its valid exit conditions.
STATE-003
Every top-level state shall define which operator controls are available.
STATE-004
Every top-level state shall define which simulation modules continue updating.
STATE-005
Every state transition shall generate a named event.
STATE-006
Invalid state transitions shall be rejected and recorded in the debug log.
STATE-007
Terminal disaster states shall prevent normal operation from resuming unless a specific recovery path is defined.
9.3 Offline State
While offline:
•	the active reaction shall not produce power;
•	the reactor chamber should appear dark or inactive;
•	the simulation clock may continue updating recovery and environmental processes;
•	superstructure recovery may occur according to the recovery requirements;
•	controls unrelated to startup or maintenance should remain unavailable;
•	required startup conditions shall remain visible to the operator.
