10.1 General Core Variables
The core shall include the following general variables:
containmentFieldRadius
Represents the effective radius of the containment field.
Required definition:
•	Unit: [metres or fictional normalized unit]
•	Minimum: [TBD]
•	Maximum: [TBD]
•	Normal operating range: [TBD]
•	Primary source: stabilizer system
•	Primary effects: event-horizon containment, chamber safety, beam compatibility
containmentFieldStrength
Represents the current power or intensity of the containment field.
The system shall define:
•	safe annihilation-stage range;
•	safe dark-fusion-stage range;
•	minimum required strength for each reactor state;
•	power consumption curve;
•	overload threshold;
•	relationship to field stability.
containmentFieldStability
Represents the field’s resistance to fluctuation or collapse.
Low field stability shall increase the probability or severity of containment-related faults.
planetOrbitalInfluenceSuppression
Represents the stabilizer’s ability to suppress the reactor’s gravitational or orbital influence.
The value shall decrease during a singularity containment breach.
radiation
Represents the reactor’s current fictional radiation output.
Radiation may affect:
•	chamber danger;
•	environmental effects;
•	alarms;
•	player damage;
•	display readings;
•	failure severity.
10.2 Annihilation-Stage Variables
The annihilation system shall include:
•	annihilationPowerGW
•	antimatterPercent
•	matterPercent
•	fuelSaturation
•	antimatterDominance
•	matterDominance
•	stellarRadius
•	singularity
Spelling and naming shall be normalized before implementation. For example, antimatterDorminace should become antimatterDominance.
10.3 Matter-Antimatter Equilibrium
The system shall calculate an equilibrium score representing the balance between matter and antimatter.
ANN-001
The equilibrium score shall use a documented calculation.
ANN-002
An equilibrium score below approximately 20% should cause either matter dominance or antimatter dominance.
ANN-003
Dominance shall reduce total annihilation efficiency.
ANN-004
Antimatter dominance shall create a greater containment risk than matter dominance.
ANN-005
The operator shall be able to control matter and antimatter together through a main injection control.
ANN-006
The operator shall also be able to adjust matter and antimatter separately through fine controls.
ANN-007
Automatic AN-Fuel injection shall only be available after the required equilibrium condition is met.
ANN-008
The equilibrium score, current dominance, and injection rates shall be visible to the operator.
10.4 Dark-Fusion-Stage Variables
The dark-fusion system shall include:
•	influxTW
•	outfluxTW
•	storedFluxGWh
•	energySaturation
•	expellingEnergyGW
•	catalyzerPower
•	annihilationFusionFactor
•	nucleogenesisRate
•	eventHorizonRadius
•	planetOrbitalInfluence
•	finalEnergyExportTW
10.5 Energy Saturation
DFR-ES-001
Energy saturation shall represent the balance between reactor influx, outflux, storage, containment, and energy expulsion.
DFR-ES-002
Energy saturation shall not be changed directly by a control unless the control is explicitly a debug or timeline override.
DFR-ES-003
Operator controls shall influence energy saturation indirectly through modeled variables such as influx, stabilizer power, catalyzer activity, and export.
DFR-ES-004
The system shall define at least the following energy-saturation thresholds:
•	low warning threshold;
•	stall threshold;
•	normal operating range;
•	high warning threshold;
•	maximum safe threshold;
•	integrity-damage threshold;
•	runaway-fusion threshold.
DFR-ES-005
Crossing a threshold shall generate a corresponding event.
DFR-ES-006
Threshold behavior should use hysteresis where required to prevent alarms from rapidly switching on and off.
