 11. Stabilizer and Containment Requirements
11.1 Stabilizer Variables
The stabilizer and superstructure system shall include:
•	temperature
•	integrity
•	wasteHeatMW
•	coolantCirculationRate
•	subsystemEffectiveness
•	stabilizerPower
•	stabilizerConsumptionGW
•	stabilizerMalfunctionPercent
•	directorBeamPrecision
•	directorBeamDirection
•	lensXOffset
•	lensYOffset
•	lensZOffset
•	directorBeamAutoAlign
•	finalEnergyExportTW
11.2 Stabilizer Behavior
STAB-001
Increasing stabilizer power shall increase containment capability.
STAB-002
Increasing stabilizer power shall increase electrical consumption.
STAB-003
The stabilizer shall have a lower power ceiling when no dark-fusion reaction is active.
STAB-004
The stabilizer shall permit a higher operating range during dark-fusion operation.
STAB-005
Low subsystem effectiveness shall increase stabilizer malfunction percentage.
STAB-006
Initial stabilizer malfunction should increase power consumption.
STAB-007
More severe stabilizer malfunction shall reduce containment stability or effective stabilizer output.
STAB-008
Stabilizer malfunction percentage shall recover gradually when its causes are removed.
STAB-009
The system shall define whether recovery can occur during operation, shutdown, or both.
11.3 Subsystem Effectiveness
Subsystem effectiveness shall represent the combined effect of heat, damage, coolant performance, and subsystem faults.
Subsystem effectiveness may affect:
•	Catalyzers;
•	Stabilizer;
•	heat exchangers;
•	automatic beam alignment;
•	fuel enrichment machinery;
•	sensor accuracy;
•	control response.
The final implementation shall define whether subsystem effectiveness is:
•	one shared global value;
•	one value per subsystem;
•	or a combination of global and subsystem-specific values.
