12. Director Beam Requirements
12.1 Beam Activation
BEAM-001
The director beam shall be required during manual annihilation-stage startup.
BEAM-002
The beam shall not operate safely above its defined containment-field compatibility limit during early startup.
BEAM-003
Attempting to fire the beam above that limit shall trip the stabilizer and apply defined integrity damage.
12.2 Precision and Direction
directorBeamDirection shall be represented as a normalized three-dimensional vector.
The beam direction shall be affected by small disturbances.
The operator shall adjust three lens offsets:
•	lensXOffset
•	lensYOffset
•	lensZOffset
The purpose of lens adjustment shall be to align the director beam with its target direction.
BEAM-004
Director-beam precision shall be displayed as a percentage.
BEAM-005
Imprecision above the defined safe threshold shall cause integrity damage.
BEAM-006
Damage caused by imprecision shall scale with reactor power or beam power.
BEAM-007
Automatic alignment shall only be enabled when precision is within its activation range.
BEAM-008
Automatic alignment effectiveness shall decrease with subsystem effectiveness.
BEAM-009
Automatic alignment shall disable itself when imprecision exceeds approximately 6%, unless a different tested value is selected.
BEAM-010
Manual startup shall require precision below approximately 1% before full containment throttling is permitted.
