13. Catalyzer Requirements
13.1 Quantity
The reactor shall contain six Dark Fusion Catalyzers.
13.2 Catalyzer Variables
Each Catalyzer shall maintain:
•	unique identifier;
•	current mode;
•	throttle;
•	fuel-cell percentage;
•	submitted power;
•	malfunction status;
•	subsystem effectiveness;
•	installed stasis-cell status, if applicable;
•	temperature, if modeled individually;
•	readiness state.
13.3 Modes
Each Catalyzer shall support:
•	OFFLINE
•	PASSIVE
•	ACTIVE
•	ANNIHILATE
•	CATALYZE
The exact distinction between PASSIVE and ACTIVE shall be documented before implementation.
13.4 Catalyzer Behavior
CAT-001
A Catalyzer shall only perform behavior associated with its current mode.
CAT-002
Passive mode shall use its throttle setting.
CAT-003
Annihilate mode shall support large-scale annihilation-stage startup.
CAT-004
Catalyze mode shall support dark-fusion ignition and sustained dark-fusion operation.
CAT-005
Catalyzer performance shall be affected by fuel-cell percentage.
CAT-006
Catalyzer performance shall be affected by subsystem effectiveness.
CAT-007
Low subsystem effectiveness may cause a Catalyzer malfunction.
CAT-008
A malfunctioning Catalyzer shall provide visible and audible feedback.
CAT-009
The simulation shall define whether one Catalyzer failure prevents ignition or merely reduces performance.
CAT-010
Each Catalyzer shall be individually addressable for debugging and future control-room interfaces.
