17. Startup Requirements
17.1 Startup Modes
The reactor shall support:
•	automatic startup;
•	manual startup.
The selected startup mode shall be communicated to all relevant modules.
17.2 Shared Startup Preconditions
Before either startup method can be authorized, the system shall check:
•	AN-Fuel availability;
•	required fuel-cell installation;
•	DECAOS mainframe status;
•	reactor state;
•	superstructure integrity;
•	stabilizer availability;
•	critical subsystem faults;
•	whether another startup or shutdown sequence is already active.
The final specification shall distinguish between:
•	conditions that block authorization;
•	conditions that permit authorization but create additional risk;
•	conditions that produce a warning only.
17.3 Facility Phone and Authorization
START-AUTH-001
The operator shall be able to call extension 7472 through the facility phone.
START-AUTH-002
The phone interface shall provide automatic and manual startup options.
START-AUTH-003
A startup request shall create an authorization state.
START-AUTH-004
The authorization response may be delayed for presentation purposes.
START-AUTH-005
Automatic startup may have an approximately 20% denial chance.
START-AUTH-006
Manual startup may have an approximately 30% denial chance.
START-AUTH-007
A denial shall provide a selected external reason through DECAOS or the phone system.
START-AUTH-008
The denial system should be configurable or disableable for testing and accessibility.
START-AUTH-009
Repeated denial behavior shall be designed to avoid unnecessarily preventing players from accessing the reactor.
17.4 Triple Startup Levers
START-LEV-001
The reactor shall use three startup levers.
START-LEV-002
The system shall define whether the levers must be activated simultaneously, within a time window, or in a sequence.
START-LEV-003
The current state of each lever shall be visible to the server.
START-LEV-004
Invalid lever activation shall provide feedback.
START-LEV-005
The lever system shall not accidentally trigger both startup and shutdown.
17.5 Automatic Startup
The automatic startup flow shall approximately follow this sequence:
1.	Check shared startup preconditions.
2.	Request automatic startup through extension 7472.
3.	Activate the three startup levers.
4.	Await authorization.
5.	Begin the startup reactive timeline.
6.	Lock controls that are managed by the timeline.
7.	Deploy the reactor machinery.
8.	Start the stabilizer and containment field.
9.	Activate the director beam.
10.	Establish matter-antimatter injection.
11.	Establish the required equilibrium and fuel saturation.
12.	Activate Catalyzers in annihilate mode.
13.	Confirm dark-fusion readiness.
14.	Divert district power to the reactor.
15.	Activate Catalyzers in catalyze mode.
16.	Establish dark-fusion output.
17.	Return power to the district after output exceeds the defined threshold.
18.	Unlock normal-operation controls.
START-AUTO-001
The reactive timeline shall respond to defined major failures.
START-AUTO-002
A detected major failure shall stop or suspend timeline control.
START-AUTO-003
When timeline control is released, the simulation shall resume from a state consistent with the physical sequence already completed.
START-AUTO-004
DECAOS shall instruct the operator about the required manual response.
START-AUTO-005
The timeline may temporarily override simulation values only when necessary to synchronize major audiovisual events.
START-AUTO-006
All timeline overrides shall be explicitly documented.
START-AUTO-007
A timeline override shall not leave the reactor in an invalid state when the sequence is interrupted.
17.6 Manual Startup
The manual startup flow shall approximately require the operator to:
1.	Check AN-Fuel and fuel-cell readiness.
2.	Request manual startup through extension 7472.
3.	Await authorization.
4.	Deploy the reactor machinery.
5.	Activate the Stabilizer.
6.	Generate a low-strength containment field.
7.	Activate the director beam.
8.	Correct beam imprecision using lens controls.
9.	Enable automatic alignment when permitted.
10.	Increase containment-field strength.
11.	Begin main matter-antimatter injection.
12.	Balance matter and antimatter using fine controls.
13.	Reach the required equilibrium.
14.	Enable automatic AN-Fuel injection.
15.	Set the fuel-saturation target.
16.	Activate Catalyzers in annihilate mode.
17.	Reach the required annihilation power and fuel saturation.
18.	Prime the Dark Fusion Key.
19.	Initiate the dark-fusion stage.
20.	Divert district power to the reactor.
21.	Activate Catalyzers in catalyze mode.
22.	Wait for power production to exceed the minimum return threshold.
23.	Restore power to the district.
24.	Enter normal operation.
17.7 Dark-Fusion Ignition Conditions
The Dark Fusion initiation control shall remain locked until all mandatory conditions are met.
Initial proposed conditions:
•	Dark Fusion Key is primed;
•	fuel saturation is at least approximately 80%;
•	annihilation power exceeds approximately 500 GW;
•	required Catalyzers are available;
•	containment stability is sufficient;
•	beam precision is sufficient;
•	no blocking fault exists;
•	reactor is in the correct annihilation substate.
The exact thresholds shall be configurable for balancing.
