Source: Manual startup design
Requirement:
The system shall prevent the operator from increasing containment-field strength above the startup beam-compatibility limit while director-beam imprecision exceeds 1%.
Rationale:
The director beam must be correctly aligned before the containment field reaches full startup strength. This creates an operator task and prevents the startup sequence from skipping beam alignment.
Preconditions:
•	reactor is in manual startup;
•	stabilizer is active;
•	director beam is active;
•	dark fusion has not been initiated.
Trigger:
The operator attempts to increase containment-field strength above the beam-compatibility limit.
Expected Behavior:
If beam imprecision is 1% or lower, the containment-field control shall operate normally.
If beam imprecision is above 1%, the control input shall be rejected or limited.
Failure Behavior:
If the system allows the field to exceed the compatibility limit due to malfunction or forced override, the stabilizer shall trip and the superstructure shall receive damage.
Operator Feedback:
•	containment control displays a lock or warning;
•	DECAOS announces that director alignment is insufficient;
•	the beam-precision display highlights the current error;
•	a failed forced attempt produces a trip alarm.
Acceptance Test:
1.	Begin manual startup.
2.	Set director-beam imprecision to 4%.
3.	Attempt to increase containment strength above the compatibility limit.
4.	Verify that the normal control is rejected.
5.	Set imprecision to 0.8%.
6.	Repeat the action.
7.	Verify that containment strength increases.
8.	Force the containment value above the limit through a debug command while imprecision is 4%.
9.	Verify that the stabilizer trips and integrity damage occurs.
Dependencies:
•	Director Beam module;
•	Stabilizer module;
•	Manual Startup controller;
•	DECAOS;
•	alarm system;
•	control-room displays.
Open Questions:
•	Should the normal control be completely locked or merely slowed?
•	How much integrity damage should a trip cause?
•	Should beam power also affect trip severity?
